{"query":"The umbilical cord should not be cut until 1 hour after birth or they baby will not have enough blood right after birth. original source fact check","results":[{"position":1,"site_name":"www.tommys.org","snippet":"The cord should not be clamped earlier than 1 minute after birth. You can have delayed cord clamping even if you have help to deliver the placenta after giving ...","title":"Delayed (optimal) cord clamping - Tommy's","url":"https://www.tommys.org/pregnancy-information/giving-birth/delayed-cord-clamping-optimal"},{"position":2,"site_name":"pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov","snippet":"The World Health Organization recommends that the umbilical cord not be clamped earlier than 1 minute after birth in term or preterm newborns.","title":"Time to Cut the Cord - PMC - NIH","url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6353264/"},{"position":3,"site_name":"www.healthychildren.org","snippet":"Even after delayed cord clamping and cutting, some blood still remains in the cord and placenta. This leftover blood can also help babies who ...","title":"Your Baby's Umbilical Cord: 5 Surprising Facts for New ...","url":"https://www.healthychildren.org/English/ages-stages/prenatal/delivery-beyond/Pages/your-babys-umbilical-cord-5-surprising-facts-for-new-and-expectant-parents.aspx"},{"position":4,"site_name":"www.mayoclinichealthsystem.org","snippet":"Waiting 30–60 seconds after birth is considered the proper cord clamping time frame due to the health benefits for your baby. For babies born ...","title":"Delayed umbilical cord clamping - Mayo Clinic Health System","url":"https://www.mayoclinichealthsystem.org/hometown-health/speaking-of-health/delayed-umbilical-cord-clamping-benefits"},{"position":5,"site_name":"www.nhs.uk","snippet":"Your newborn's umbilical cord takes about a week to dry out and drop off. Keep it clean and dry until it does. If you notice any bleeding or ...","title":"Getting to know your newborn - NHS","url":"https://www.nhs.uk/pregnancy/labour-and-birth/getting-to-know-your-newborn/"},{"position":6,"site_name":"www.hopkinsmedicine.org","snippet":"However, doctors recommend waiting 30 to 60 seconds before cutting the umbilical cord. This helps your baby get some extra benefits, like more blood and oxygen.","title":"Care of the Baby in the Delivery Room | Johns Hopkins Medicine","url":"https://www.hopkinsmedicine.org/health/conditions-and-diseases/care-of-the-baby-in-the-delivery-room"},{"position":7,"site_name":"www.reddit.com","snippet":"No. The cord isn't cut at the belly button, it's cut an inch or two away. The stub falls off the belly button naturally after about a week, just ...","title":"ELI5 what would happen to the umbilical cord after birth if not ...","url":"https://www.reddit.com/r/explainlikeimfive/comments/1776fxb/eli5_what_would_happen_to_the_umbilical_cord/"},{"position":8,"site_name":"www.facebook.com","snippet":"⠀ ⠀ In the U.S. today, cutting the umbilical cord 10 to 15 seconds after your child is born is the standard practice. However, before the mid- ...","title":"This decision happens seconds after birth… and it matters ...","url":"https://www.facebook.com/dryoun/posts/this-decision-happens-seconds-after-birth-and-it-matters-doctorreact-umbilicalco/1453130419500483/"},{"position":9,"site_name":"www.mayoclinic.org","snippet":"After birth, the umbilical cord isn't needed anymore. So, a healthcare professional clamps and cuts it soon after your baby is born. This ...","title":"Umbilical cord care: Do's and don'ts for parents - Mayo Clinic","url":"https://www.mayoclinic.org/healthy-lifestyle/infant-and-toddler-health/in-depth/umbilical-cord/art-20048250"},{"position":10,"site_name":"americanpregnancy.org","snippet":"Delayed cord clamping allows more blood to be passed to a premature baby that has just been delivered. Learn the benefits and risks.","title":"Delayed Cord Clamping | American Pregnancy Association","url":"https://americanpregnancy.org/giving-birth/delayed-cord-clamping/"}],"total_result